{0 Shared authentication profiles}

{!Jmap_eio.Profile} gives a name to a session URL and its credential. The
command-line tools, tutorial programs and Mosaic share the same store, so a
login saved by one can be selected by the others.

{1 Construct a profile}

A bearer profile holds a service-issued API token. Construction validates the
fields without accessing the filesystem or network.

{x@ocaml[
# module Profile = Jmap_eio.Profile;;
module Profile = Jmap_eio.Profile
# let personal =
    Profile.v ~name:"personal"
      ~session_url:"https://api.example.com/.well-known/jmap"
      (Profile.Bearer "example-token") |> Result.get_ok;;
val personal : Profile.t = <abstr>
# Profile.name personal;;
- : string = "personal"
# Profile.session_url personal;;
- : string = "https://api.example.com/.well-known/jmap"
]x}

For Basic authentication, use [Profile.Basic { user; password }]. Its username
and password are stored separately. A profile name is a filename in the store;
paths and traversal components are rejected.

{x@ocaml[
# Profile.valid_name "../personal";;
- : bool = false
# Result.is_ok
    (Profile.v ~name:"oracle"
       ~session_url:"http://localhost:18080/.well-known/jmap"
       (Profile.Basic { user = "user1"; password = "x" }));;
- : bool = true
]x}

{1 Save and load}

Define a save operation, then call [save env personal] within an Eio environment:

{[
let save env personal =
  let ( let* ) = Result.bind in
  let* store = Profile.xdg_store env in
  Profile.save store personal
]}

{!Jmap_eio.Profile.xdg_store} selects
[$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/jmap/profiles], falling back to
[$HOME/.config/jmap/profiles] when the XDG path is unset or relative.
{!Jmap_eio.Profile.save} atomically creates or replaces the named profile.
New directories have mode [0700] and files have mode [0600]. An existing store
directory with group or other permissions is rejected without changing its
mode. Credentials are stored in plaintext; {!Jmap_eio.Profile.load} rejects
nonregular, oversized or overly permissive files. {!Jmap_eio.Profile.pp} redacts
the secret.

{!Jmap_eio.Profile.load} reads one name and {!Jmap_eio.Profile.list} reads the
valid profiles in name order. A test or confined application can use
{!Jmap_eio.Profile.of_directory} to select another directory through its Eio
filesystem capability.

[examples/0-profiles/profiles.ml] is a runnable example of these operations.
Its [save] command uses {!Jmap_eio.Auth.read_secret_file} to import a private
key file. This copies the secret into the profile; it does not store a path to
the original key file or pick up its later changes.

{1 Connect by name}

{!Jmap_eio.Profile.connect_name} loads a profile and fetches the session using
its credential. The client lives within the switch passed to it.

{[
let connect name =
  Eio_main.run @@ fun env ->
  Eio.Switch.run @@ fun sw ->
  match Jmap_eio.Profile.connect_name ~sw ~timeout:30. env name with
  | Error error -> Fmt.epr "%a@." Jmap_eio.Profile.pp_error error
  | Ok client ->
      let session = Jmap_eio.Client.session client in
      Fmt.pr "Connected as %s@."
        (Jmap_eio.Cli.terminal_text session.username)
]}

[connect "personal"] uses the saved login. A profile chooses the login, not
an account. Choose an account from the session,
for example with {!Jmap.Proto.Session.primary_account_for}, after connecting.
Cleartext credentials require [~allow_insecure:true] on each connection; this
choice is not stored in the profile. Use it for the local HTTP oracle.

{1 Use the tutorial commands}

The commands built with {!Jmap_eio.Cli.val-main} already accept [--profile] and
[JMAP_PROFILE]. After saving [personal], run:

{v
dune exec -- examples/1-session/session.exe --profile personal
dune exec -- examples/3-inbox/inbox.exe --profile personal
v}

A command-line connection setting wins over its environment value, which wins
over the profile field. Unset [JMAP_SESSION_URL], [JMAP_API_KEY],
[JMAP_API_KEY_FILE] and [JMAP_AUTH] when the profile should supply the whole
login. [--account] or [JMAP_ACCOUNT_ID] selects a different account reached by
the same credential. The direct [Profile.connect_name] API uses the stored
profile without merging these command-line overrides.

{!Jmap_eio.Cli.profile_term} supplies only the profile selector for programs
with a command structure of their own. The [connect] subcommand in
[examples/0-profiles/] demonstrates it; the other examples use [Cli.main] to
connect and select the account together.
